        "root_concepts": "[aging]",
        "section": "demography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Population Aging",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "1. AGE 65 IS ARBITRARY:\n   Bismarck set pension age at 70 (later 65) in 1889 when German LE was ~40.\n   Today, a 65-year-old in a rich country has ~19 more years of life expectancy\n   and often full cognitive and physical capacity."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-AGING.md#017",
      "path": [
        "06-AGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:demography:06-aging, git-history:demography:06-aging]",
        "canonical_path": "demography/06-AGING.md",
        "concepts": "[aging]",
        "current_path": "demography/06-AGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:demography:aging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "demography",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[aging]",
        "section": "demography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Population Aging",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "2. LABOR FORCE PARTICIPATION VARIES:\n   Many people \"retire\" before 65 (early retirement incentives).\n   Many work past 65 (self-employed professionals, poor health insurance).\n   Actual economic contributions matter more than age."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-AGING.md#018",
      "path": [
        "06-AGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:demography:06-aging, git-history:demography:06-aging]",
        "canonical_path": "demography/06-AGING.md",
        "concepts": "[aging]",
        "current_path": "demography/06-AGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:demography:aging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "demography",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[aging]",
        "section": "demography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Population Aging",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "3. HEALTH STATUS CHANGING:\n   Today's 75-year-old is healthier than 75-year-old was in 1990.\n   Rowe & Kahn \"successful aging\": active, engaged, cognitively intact."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-AGING.md#019",
      "path": [
        "06-AGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
